WEBVTT

00:09.592 --> 00:11.302
[insects chirping]

00:22.063 --> 00:23.898
[Joyce yelling] Let me out of here!

00:25.483 --> 00:27.610
Somebody, please!

00:29.320 --> 00:30.572
[grunts]

00:30.655 --> 00:32.824
Let me out!

00:33.867 --> 00:35.118
[door unlocking]

00:37.203 --> 00:38.955
[Joyce breathing heavily]

00:53.219 --> 00:54.637
[Dr. Brenner] Your son.

00:55.638 --> 00:57.932
We know you've been in contact with him.

01:00.226 --> 01:03.063
- [stammering] You have to let me--
- When...

01:04.230 --> 01:06.775
and how did you make contact with him?

01:08.109 --> 01:09.569
- What?
- Hmm?

01:11.613 --> 01:12.864
Six.

01:13.948 --> 01:15.241
What?

01:16.659 --> 01:17.869
Six.

01:19.412 --> 01:22.165
Six people have been taken this week.

01:23.374 --> 01:26.795
This... thing that took your son...

01:28.546 --> 01:30.840
[softly] we don't really understand it.

01:30.924 --> 01:33.426
But its behavior is predictable.

01:34.469 --> 01:37.597
Like all animals...

01:39.682 --> 01:40.934
it eats.

01:42.477 --> 01:44.187
It will take more sons.

01:45.230 --> 01:46.272
More daughters.

01:47.649 --> 01:48.942
I want to save them.

01:50.568 --> 01:52.487
I want to save your son.

01:53.988 --> 01:55.156
But I can't do that.

01:56.074 --> 01:57.325
Not without your help.

01:57.408 --> 01:58.618
Stop.

02:02.497 --> 02:04.290
I know who you are.

02:04.958 --> 02:06.835
I know what you've done.

02:08.128 --> 02:11.131
You took my boy away from me!

02:11.214 --> 02:14.968
You left him in that place to die!

02:15.051 --> 02:17.053
You faked his death!

02:18.763 --> 02:20.265
We had a funeral.

02:20.348 --> 02:22.725
We buried him.

02:23.893 --> 02:26.896
And now you're asking for my help?

02:31.025 --> 02:32.569
Go to hell.

02:34.070 --> 02:35.196
- [electricity crackling]
- [groaning]

02:38.199 --> 02:41.119
- [breathing heavily]
- Okay, now what do you know?

02:41.202 --> 02:42.787
I'm sorry.

02:43.872 --> 02:44.873
Did I stutter?

02:46.499 --> 02:48.001
I told you.

02:48.084 --> 02:49.460
Everything.

02:49.544 --> 02:50.879
[electricity crackling]

02:53.298 --> 02:55.133
What do you know?

02:55.216 --> 02:56.718
[panting]

02:56.801 --> 02:59.137
I know you do experiments
on kidnapped little kids,

02:59.220 --> 03:01.598
whose parents' brains
you've turned to mush.

03:02.473 --> 03:04.267
And I know you went
a little too far this time

03:04.350 --> 03:06.269
and you messed up in a big way.

03:07.270 --> 03:10.398
I mean, you really messed up,
didn't you? Big time.

03:10.481 --> 03:12.400
That's why you're trying
to cover your tracks.

03:13.610 --> 03:16.446
You killed Benny Hammond,
you faked Will Byers' death.

03:16.529 --> 03:18.948
You made it look like
that little girl just ran away.

03:19.032 --> 03:20.450
See, I told you.

03:21.701 --> 03:24.120
- I know everything.
- All right, who are you working with?

03:24.954 --> 03:26.414
Nobody.

03:26.497 --> 03:28.666
But I did give all this
over to my friend at the Times.

03:28.750 --> 03:30.460
He's gonna blow this thing wide open.
[chuckles]

03:30.543 --> 03:33.087
- [electricity crackling]
- [groans]

03:35.715 --> 03:37.133
[grunting]

03:39.344 --> 03:40.929
You're just a junkie.

03:41.012 --> 03:44.724
A small town cop
who had a really bad week.

03:44.807 --> 03:47.060
Took one too many pills this time.

03:50.772 --> 03:52.941
You made a mistake coming back here.

03:53.024 --> 03:54.609
No, I didn't.

03:56.486 --> 03:57.946
Here's what's gonna happen.

03:59.656 --> 04:01.574
You're gonna let me and Joyce Byers go...

04:02.825 --> 04:04.869
you're gonna give us anything we need,

04:04.953 --> 04:06.996
and we're gonna find her son.

04:08.081 --> 04:11.793
And then we're gonna forget
that any of this ever happened.

04:11.876 --> 04:14.003
Oh, is that right?

04:15.421 --> 04:16.589
Yeah.

04:18.383 --> 04:19.759
That's right.

04:33.231 --> 04:35.483
Nancy? Jonathan?

04:39.904 --> 04:41.489
[door closes]

04:42.365 --> 04:44.450
- They're gone.
- What?

04:44.534 --> 04:45.827
Nancy and Jonathan.
His car's gone.

04:45.910 --> 04:47.453
They're probably
just sucking face somewhere.

04:47.537 --> 04:49.455
- [Lucas] Gross.
- No. No way!

04:49.539 --> 04:50.623
Did they go with the chief?

04:50.707 --> 04:51.708
I don't know.

04:52.417 --> 04:53.418
No.

04:54.252 --> 04:56.796
What? Did you see them?
Do you know where they went?

04:58.131 --> 05:00.091
- Yes.
- Where? Where did they go?

05:02.885 --> 05:04.220
Demogorgon.

06:23.883 --> 06:24.884
[sighs]

06:52.245 --> 06:53.871
Where's the girl?

06:55.623 --> 06:57.208
[inhales deeply]

06:58.334 --> 06:59.585
[exhales]

07:01.462 --> 07:03.339
You gotta give me your word.

07:05.174 --> 07:07.426
Nobody's ever gonna find out about this.

07:08.719 --> 07:12.181
And those other three kids, those boys,
you're gonna leave them alone.

07:14.600 --> 07:16.310
Then I'll tell you.

07:18.771 --> 07:21.607
Tell you where
your little science experiment is.

07:30.366 --> 07:31.367
[sighs]

07:37.832 --> 07:39.375
[gasps]

07:46.716 --> 07:48.134
I don't understand.

07:48.217 --> 07:49.886
We came to an agreement.

07:49.969 --> 07:51.554
What?

07:51.637 --> 07:54.182
Look, everything that's happened here
and everything that's gonna happen,

07:54.265 --> 07:55.683
we don't talk about.

07:55.766 --> 07:56.976
You want Will back?

07:58.060 --> 07:59.687
This place had nothing to do with it.

08:00.730 --> 08:03.316
That's the deal.
You got it?

08:12.700 --> 08:14.243
What is this?

08:14.327 --> 08:17.163
Protection.
The atmosphere is toxic.

08:17.246 --> 08:19.624
[stutters] But my son's in there. He...

08:19.707 --> 08:20.833
Put it on.

08:36.224 --> 08:37.600
[Connie] I'm telling you,
this is a mistake.

08:37.683 --> 08:39.727
[Dr. Brenner] It's gone.
Isn't that what you wanted?

08:39.810 --> 08:41.562
And if they find the boy?

08:41.646 --> 08:43.231
That's not gonna happen.

09:07.296 --> 09:08.881
[low growling]

09:38.995 --> 09:40.997
[theme music playing]

10:54.153 --> 10:55.946
[Joyce breathing heavily]

11:03.037 --> 11:04.413
[Hopper] Hey, you all right?

11:04.497 --> 11:05.539
[Joyce] Yeah.

11:05.623 --> 11:07.291
[Hopper echoing]
I need you to relax, okay?

11:08.209 --> 11:10.795
I want you to slow down your breathing,
take deep breaths.

11:10.878 --> 11:12.963
In and out.

11:14.465 --> 11:15.758
Deep breath in...

11:16.759 --> 11:17.843
and out.

11:18.803 --> 11:21.472
In and out.

11:22.264 --> 11:25.810
- In and out.
- It's troll's favorite food!

11:25.893 --> 11:27.561
- [growling] Princess!
- No, Daddy! No, Daddy!

11:27.645 --> 11:31.690
- Roasted princess with paprika and gravy!
- No! No, Daddy. No, Daddy.

11:31.774 --> 11:34.026
[Hopper growling]

11:34.110 --> 11:36.112
- [Sarah breathing heavily]
- Whoa, hey!

11:36.195 --> 11:37.530
Hey.

11:37.613 --> 11:38.989
- [Sarah breathing heavily]
- You all right?

11:39.073 --> 11:40.366
- What's going on?
- Whoa.

11:40.449 --> 11:42.535
- What happened? What happened?
- I don't know. I don't know.

11:43.577 --> 11:45.037
Hey, you all right?

11:45.121 --> 11:46.163
Whoa, whoa, whoa.

11:46.247 --> 11:48.249
- Relax, relax. Honey, honey.
- [panting]

11:48.332 --> 11:50.251
Honey, just breathe.
Breathe, breathe, breathe.

11:50.334 --> 11:53.045
In and out.
Slow, slow, slow.

11:53.129 --> 11:54.713
[inhaling deeply]

11:54.797 --> 11:56.632
In and out with me.

11:56.715 --> 11:57.716
In...

11:59.468 --> 12:01.762
- You okay?
- [breathing heavily] Yeah.

12:01.846 --> 12:02.972
Yeah.

12:23.701 --> 12:24.743
Remember...

12:24.827 --> 12:27.580
- Straight into Will's room. And--
- Don't step on the trap.

12:27.663 --> 12:29.081
Wait for the yo-yo to move.

12:29.165 --> 12:30.624
Then...

12:32.460 --> 12:33.586
All right.

12:34.503 --> 12:35.504
You ready?

12:37.256 --> 12:38.299
Ready.

12:40.342 --> 12:41.510
[Jonathan] On three.

12:42.470 --> 12:43.554
One...

12:44.930 --> 12:46.223
two...

12:47.475 --> 12:48.476
You don't have to do this--

12:48.559 --> 12:49.560
Jonathan, stop talking.

12:49.643 --> 12:50.811
- I'm just saying, you don't have to--
- Three.

12:51.562 --> 12:54.523
[Mike] Guys, guys! This is crazy.

12:54.607 --> 12:55.900
We can't just wait around.

12:55.983 --> 12:58.277
Mike, in case you forgot,
we're still fugitives.

12:58.360 --> 12:59.737
The bad men are still looking for us.

12:59.820 --> 13:01.697
Yeah, and we don't even know
where your sister is.

13:01.780 --> 13:02.781
El can find them.

13:02.865 --> 13:03.866
Mike, look at her.

13:04.825 --> 13:06.619
I still think we should stick
to the chief's plan.

13:06.702 --> 13:10.289
Exactly. We stay here,
keep El out of sight and keep her safe.

13:10.372 --> 13:12.166
That's the most important thing, remember?

13:12.249 --> 13:14.168
Besides, she's okay.
She's with Jonathan.

13:14.251 --> 13:16.670
Yeah, and she's kind of
a badass now, so...

13:17.630 --> 13:20.049
Well, where are you going?
You just said stick to the plan!

13:20.132 --> 13:22.510
I am. I'm just gonna go get
some chocolate pudding.

13:22.593 --> 13:24.678
I'm telling you,
Lunch Lady Phyllis hoards that shit.

13:24.762 --> 13:26.013
[Mike] Are you serious?

13:26.096 --> 13:27.765
El needs to be recharged!

13:30.059 --> 13:31.143
[door opens]

13:32.811 --> 13:33.854
[door shuts]

13:46.283 --> 13:47.535
[faint creaking]

13:48.702 --> 13:49.995
Did you hear that?

13:52.748 --> 13:54.250
It's just the wind.

13:59.922 --> 14:01.382
Don't worry.

14:01.465 --> 14:04.802
My mom, she said the lights speak
when it comes.

14:04.885 --> 14:05.970
Speak?

14:06.637 --> 14:08.097
Blink.

14:08.180 --> 14:10.266
Think of them as alarms.

14:19.316 --> 14:20.818
Is that too tight?

14:21.735 --> 14:23.195
[stutters] No, it's fine.

14:23.279 --> 14:24.488
Thanks.

14:35.958 --> 14:37.042
Nancy?

14:39.003 --> 14:40.504
Yeah?

14:42.256 --> 14:43.340
- [banging on door]
- [both gasp]

14:44.675 --> 14:46.468
[Steve] Jonathan?

14:46.552 --> 14:48.888
Are you there, man?
It's... it's Steve!

14:49.680 --> 14:51.473
Listen, I just want to talk!

14:51.557 --> 14:52.766
[banging on door continues]

14:54.810 --> 14:56.186
- Steve, listen to me.
- Hey. Nancy, what--

14:56.312 --> 14:58.689
- You need to leave.
- I'm not trying to start anything, okay?

14:58.772 --> 14:59.940
I don't care about that.
You need to leave.

15:00.024 --> 15:03.360
[stammering] No, no, no.
Listen, I messed up, okay?

15:03.444 --> 15:05.112
I messed... I messed up.

15:05.195 --> 15:06.196
Okay?

15:06.280 --> 15:08.032
Really. Please.

15:08.115 --> 15:09.658
I just want to make things right.

15:10.826 --> 15:13.037
Okay? Please. Please...

15:13.954 --> 15:15.164
[stammers]

15:15.247 --> 15:16.540
Hey, what happened to your hand?

15:16.624 --> 15:17.875
Is that blood?

15:17.958 --> 15:19.710
Nothing.
[stutters] It was an accident.

15:19.793 --> 15:21.670
- Yeah, what's going on?
- Nothing.

15:21.754 --> 15:23.547
- Wait a sec. Did he do this to you?
- No.

15:23.631 --> 15:25.925
- Nancy, let me in!
- No. No! No, Steve!

15:27.259 --> 15:28.969
- What is... What the...
- You need to get out of here.

15:29.053 --> 15:30.846
- Whoa. What is all--
- Listen to me. I'm not asking you,

15:30.930 --> 15:32.473
- I'm telling you, get out of here!
- What is that smell?

15:32.556 --> 15:33.974
- Is that... is that gasoline?
- Steve, get out!

15:34.058 --> 15:36.769
[stutters] Wait.
What? What is going on?

15:36.852 --> 15:38.145
You have five seconds
to get out of here.

15:38.228 --> 15:39.647
Okay, is this a joke?
Stop. Put the gun down.

15:39.730 --> 15:41.523
- I'm doing this for you.
- Nancy.

15:41.607 --> 15:42.775
- Wait. Is this a... What is this?
- Nancy.

15:42.858 --> 15:44.860
- Three. Two.
- No, no, no! No, no!

15:44.944 --> 15:46.654
Nancy! The lights.

15:47.655 --> 15:49.531
- It's here.
- [Steve] Wait, what's here?

15:49.615 --> 15:50.616
- [Nancy] Where is it?
- Where is what? Whoa!

15:50.699 --> 15:52.201
- Easy with that!
- Where is it?

15:52.284 --> 15:53.369
I don't know.
I don't see it.

15:53.452 --> 15:54.453
Where is what?

15:54.536 --> 15:57.289
Hello? Will someone please explain to me
what the hell is going--

16:01.418 --> 16:02.419
- [monster roars]
- [Jonathan] No!

16:02.503 --> 16:04.922
Go! Go! Run! Go!

16:05.005 --> 16:06.340
[Jonathan] Get out of here!

16:07.216 --> 16:08.801
[growls]

16:08.884 --> 16:11.387
[Jonathan] Jump!
[Steve] Oh, my God! Oh, my God!

16:13.097 --> 16:14.890
Jesus! Jesus! What the hell was that?

16:14.974 --> 16:16.392
- What the hell was that?
- [both] Shut up!

16:16.475 --> 16:18.227
[monster screeching]

16:19.061 --> 16:20.354
[all panting]

16:24.316 --> 16:25.317
[Nancy] What's it doing?

16:26.360 --> 16:27.528
I don't know.

16:34.451 --> 16:35.619
[electricity jolts]

16:41.125 --> 16:42.584
Do you hear anything?

16:43.544 --> 16:44.545
No.

16:44.628 --> 16:45.838
[door opening]

17:42.186 --> 17:43.228
[Joyce echoing] Will!

17:43.312 --> 17:44.813
Will!

17:46.148 --> 17:47.691
[breathing heavily]

17:49.651 --> 17:51.612
Will!

17:56.700 --> 17:57.701
Will!

18:03.957 --> 18:05.000
[indistinct sobbing]

18:09.421 --> 18:12.591
[Hopper] "I asked Mrs. Spencer what made
them red and she said she didn't know

18:12.674 --> 18:14.551
and for pity's sake
not to ask her any more questions.

18:14.635 --> 18:16.428
She said I must have asked her
a thousand already.

18:16.512 --> 18:17.638
I suppose I had, too,

18:17.721 --> 18:20.724
but how are you gonna find things out
if you don't ask questions?

18:20.808 --> 18:22.684
And what does make roads red?

18:22.768 --> 18:24.520
'Well, I don't know,' said Matthew.

18:24.603 --> 18:27.231
It just makes me feel glad to be alive...

18:28.398 --> 18:30.526
it's such an interesting world."

18:40.369 --> 18:41.912
[sobbing]

18:47.292 --> 18:48.877
[Joyce yelling] Will!

18:52.297 --> 18:53.632
[Hopper] Will!

19:27.207 --> 19:29.042
[Steve muttering]

19:29.126 --> 19:30.919
This is crazy. This is crazy.
This is crazy.

19:31.003 --> 19:33.255
This is crazy! This is crazy!
This is crazy!

19:36.216 --> 19:38.385
What are you do--
What are you doing? Are you insane?

19:38.468 --> 19:39.636
It's going to come back!

19:39.720 --> 19:41.471
So you need to leave.

19:41.555 --> 19:43.432
Right now.

19:58.655 --> 20:00.240
[electricity pulsating]

20:04.703 --> 20:06.538
[both breathing heavily]

20:07.080 --> 20:08.290
[Nancy] Where is it?

20:08.373 --> 20:11.668
[Jonathan] Come on.
Come on, you son of a bitch.

20:11.752 --> 20:13.670
- You see it?
- No. Where--

20:13.754 --> 20:14.838
Come on.

20:15.797 --> 20:17.549
Where are you?
Come on!

20:21.094 --> 20:22.262
[low growling]

20:23.430 --> 20:24.640
- Jonathan!
- [growling]

20:24.723 --> 20:26.016
[yelps]

20:26.099 --> 20:27.434
- [groaning]
- Jonathan!

20:28.101 --> 20:29.645
Jonathan!

20:29.728 --> 20:31.730
[monster growling]

20:33.649 --> 20:36.026
Go to hell, you son of a bitch!

20:38.946 --> 20:40.030
[sputters]

20:45.577 --> 20:47.120
[gun clicking]

20:48.038 --> 20:49.498
[Steve grunting]

20:50.165 --> 20:53.001
- [Nancy] Steve!
- [monster roars]

20:54.127 --> 20:55.212
[Steve grunting]

21:04.096 --> 21:05.305
[Jonathan] He's in the trap!

21:07.891 --> 21:09.851
- He's stuck!
- [Nancy] Jonathan, now!

21:13.230 --> 21:14.773
[monster screeching]

21:18.860 --> 21:20.320
Did you hear that?

21:20.404 --> 21:22.239
[screeching continues faintly]

21:26.702 --> 21:29.371
Get back! [grunting]

21:35.794 --> 21:38.046
- [Jonathan panting]
- [all coughing]

21:44.344 --> 21:45.929
[all panting]

21:49.057 --> 21:50.892
[Nancy] Where did it go?
[Jonathan] No.

21:50.976 --> 21:52.394
It has to be dead.

21:53.353 --> 21:54.646
[panting] It has to be.

22:03.947 --> 22:05.324
[Hopper] Come on.

22:05.407 --> 22:07.284
[Joyce] Is that my house?

22:14.708 --> 22:16.376
[door creaking]

22:27.554 --> 22:29.139
[Jonathan gasps]

22:31.475 --> 22:32.601
[Jonathan sighs]

22:39.691 --> 22:41.234
[Hopper] It was hurt.

22:41.318 --> 22:42.778
[Steve panting]

23:15.644 --> 23:16.645
Mom.

23:16.728 --> 23:18.647
[Jonathan echoing] Is that you?

23:21.066 --> 23:22.192
Mom.

23:24.111 --> 23:25.362
Jonathan?

23:28.990 --> 23:30.951
[Hopper] Joyce, come on.

23:39.042 --> 23:40.502
[crackling]

23:42.379 --> 23:44.131
Where's it going?

23:45.590 --> 23:47.551
I don't think that's the monster.

23:52.848 --> 23:55.225
Found it!
I knew she was hoarding it.

23:55.308 --> 23:56.643
- I knew it.
- Yeah.

23:56.726 --> 23:58.186
Always lying, saying she's out.

23:58.270 --> 23:59.855
Bald-faced liar.

23:59.938 --> 24:03.233
Mike, I found the chocolate pudding!

24:03.316 --> 24:04.693
Okay!

24:05.694 --> 24:06.987
Are you feeling any better?

24:08.697 --> 24:10.157
[sighs]

24:10.240 --> 24:12.409
What's "putting"?

24:12.492 --> 24:14.119
[chuckles] Pudding, it's...

24:14.202 --> 24:15.745
it's this chocolate goo
you eat with a spoon.

24:16.288 --> 24:17.289
Don't worry,

24:17.372 --> 24:19.583
when all this is over,
you won't have to keep eating junk food

24:19.666 --> 24:21.293
and leftovers like a dog anymore.

24:21.376 --> 24:23.545
My mom,
she's a pretty awesome cook.

24:23.628 --> 24:25.130
She can make you whatever you like.

24:25.213 --> 24:26.506
Eggos?

24:26.590 --> 24:29.843
Well, yeah, Eggos, but real food, too.

24:31.094 --> 24:32.179
[sighs]

24:32.262 --> 24:33.680
See, I was thinking,

24:33.763 --> 24:37.017
once all this is over and Will's back
and you're not a secret anymore,

24:37.100 --> 24:39.603
my parents can get you
an actual bed for the basement.

24:39.686 --> 24:41.396
Or you can take my room if you want,

24:41.479 --> 24:44.024
since I'm down there
all the time anyways.

24:44.107 --> 24:46.234
My point is, they'll take care of you.

24:46.318 --> 24:48.028
They'll be like your new parents,

24:48.111 --> 24:50.864
and Nancy,
she'll be like your new sister.

24:51.781 --> 24:53.742
Will you be like my brother?

24:53.825 --> 24:56.536
What? No, no. [scoffs]

24:56.620 --> 24:58.163
Why "no"?

24:58.246 --> 24:59.623
Because... [sighs]

25:00.624 --> 25:01.750
'cause it's different.

25:01.833 --> 25:03.084
Why?

25:03.168 --> 25:06.213
[sighs] I mean, I don't know,
I guess it's not.

25:07.172 --> 25:08.590
It's stupid.

25:09.799 --> 25:10.884
Mike?

25:10.967 --> 25:12.135
Yeah?

25:12.219 --> 25:14.346
Friends don't lie.

25:15.430 --> 25:16.640
[sighing] Well...

25:17.807 --> 25:19.017
I was thinking...

25:19.976 --> 25:21.311
I don't know...

25:22.479 --> 25:25.148
maybe we can go
to the Snow Ball together.

25:25.232 --> 25:27.192
- "Snow Ball"?
- It's this cheesy school dance,

25:27.275 --> 25:29.986
where you go in the gym
and dance to music and stuff.

25:30.070 --> 25:32.781
I've never been, but I know you're not
supposed to go with your sister.

25:33.657 --> 25:35.575
- No?
- I mean...

25:35.659 --> 25:37.786
you can, but it'd be really weird.

25:37.869 --> 25:41.539
You go to school dances
with someone that, you know...

25:42.332 --> 25:44.125
someone that you like.

25:44.209 --> 25:46.169
- A friend?
- Not a friend.

25:46.253 --> 25:48.630
[sighs] Uh... uh...

25:49.631 --> 25:51.299
Uh, someone like a...

26:04.354 --> 26:05.897
[car approaching]

26:07.482 --> 26:09.317
Nancy.
Hold on, I'll be right back.

26:09.401 --> 26:10.735
Stay here.

26:16.700 --> 26:18.785
[tires screeching]

26:22.956 --> 26:24.958
- [tires screeching]
- [indistinct yelling]

26:26.084 --> 26:27.335
[agent] Go!

26:28.545 --> 26:29.838
You two, on me.

26:32.257 --> 26:35.093
This will charge your battery right up,
I'm telling you.

26:35.176 --> 26:37.637
- [Mike] Guys! Guys!
- What is it?

26:37.721 --> 26:40.307
[panting] They found us.

26:40.390 --> 26:42.017
[agent] We know they're here.

26:44.519 --> 26:46.646
Be advised,
west side of the building is clear.

26:49.649 --> 26:52.110
[agent] Sir, we've searched everywhere.
There's no sign of them.

26:52.193 --> 26:54.362
[indistinct radio chatter]

26:56.656 --> 26:57.699
[agent] Nothin'.

27:00.368 --> 27:02.037
Keep it locked down.

27:02.120 --> 27:03.330
[agent] All right.

27:04.456 --> 27:05.457
Kitchen.

27:06.583 --> 27:08.710
[indistinct radio chatter]

27:08.793 --> 27:10.170
[panting]

27:11.755 --> 27:12.797
How did they find us?

27:12.881 --> 27:14.382
I don't know,
but they knew we were in the gym.

27:14.466 --> 27:15.633
Lando.

27:17.552 --> 27:19.179
[agent] Got 'em!
[Mike] Go, go, go, go, go!

27:19.262 --> 27:20.430
[Lucas] Come on!

27:20.513 --> 27:21.639
[agents yelling indistinctly]

27:21.723 --> 27:23.516
- There they are. Freeze.
- [Mike] Back! Go back!

27:23.600 --> 27:25.393
[Mike] Go, go! Go left!

27:27.062 --> 27:28.938
[indistinct yelling]

27:38.323 --> 27:40.492
- [squelching]
- [choking]

27:52.754 --> 27:53.755
[Eleven thuds]

27:53.838 --> 27:56.341
[Mike panting] El, are you okay?

27:56.883 --> 27:58.009
El!

27:58.093 --> 27:59.427
- Something's wrong.
- She's just drained.

27:59.511 --> 28:01.846
No, no, no,
she won't wake up. El!

28:01.930 --> 28:03.598
El!
[echoing] El!

28:05.308 --> 28:07.018
[Hopper] There's more blood.

28:14.359 --> 28:15.652
Oh, my God.

28:18.738 --> 28:20.365
[Joyce] This way.

29:16.212 --> 29:18.173
- She's barely breathing.
- We gotta go.

29:18.256 --> 29:19.257
[Dr. Brenner] Leave her.

29:22.927 --> 29:25.138
- Step away from the child.
- [Mike] No!

29:25.221 --> 29:26.931
You want her,
you have to kill us first.

29:27.015 --> 29:28.808
- That's right!
- Eat shit!

29:28.892 --> 29:30.685
- Oh, no! No, no!
- No! No! Get off me!

29:30.810 --> 29:33.104
- [screaming] You idiot!
- No!

29:33.229 --> 29:36.316
[Dustin] Get off me!
[Mike] Ow! Let go!

29:37.317 --> 29:39.569
Eleven?
Eleven, can you hear me?

29:39.652 --> 29:40.695
Eleven?

29:41.654 --> 29:42.655
Papa?

29:42.739 --> 29:45.200
Yes, yes, it's your papa.

29:45.283 --> 29:47.118
[Mike] Get off of me. [grunts]
[Dr. Brenner] I'm here now.

29:47.202 --> 29:50.246
Let her go!
Let her go, you bastard!

29:50.330 --> 29:51.873
[whimpering]

29:51.956 --> 29:54.083
Shh, shh, you're sick.

29:54.167 --> 29:56.252
You're sick,
but I'm going to make you better.

29:56.336 --> 30:00.173
I'm going to take you back home,
where I can make you well again.

30:00.256 --> 30:02.175
Where we can make all of this better,

30:02.258 --> 30:04.177
so no one else gets hurt.

30:08.598 --> 30:09.682
Bad.

30:11.726 --> 30:12.852
Bad.

30:17.524 --> 30:19.776
Mike. Mike.

30:19.859 --> 30:21.528
- [grunts]
- Mike.

30:21.611 --> 30:22.987
[electricity spiking]

30:26.991 --> 30:28.034
Blood.

30:28.117 --> 30:29.327
What?

30:29.911 --> 30:30.954
Blood.

30:41.256 --> 30:43.007
[thudding]

30:48.263 --> 30:49.556
[screeching]

30:49.973 --> 30:51.057
Demogorgon.

30:55.103 --> 30:56.312
[Mike] Go, go, go, go, go!

30:56.437 --> 30:58.606
- [guns firing]
- [indistinct shouting]

31:00.149 --> 31:01.359
[Mike] Come on, come on.
[Lucas] Go, go!

31:02.777 --> 31:04.445
[monster screeching]

31:04.529 --> 31:06.072
[indistinct shouting]

31:08.449 --> 31:09.701
[yells]

32:07.967 --> 32:09.802
[under breath] Oh, my God.

32:34.160 --> 32:36.454
Will! Will!

32:38.665 --> 32:40.124
Will! Oh, my God!

32:40.208 --> 32:42.543
Will! Hopper!

32:42.627 --> 32:45.463
Oh, my God!
You need to help get him out!

32:46.798 --> 32:47.799
[Joyce crying] Get him out!

32:52.595 --> 32:53.680
[Joyce whimpers]

33:01.813 --> 33:03.523
- [grunts]
- [tendril hissing]

33:03.606 --> 33:05.108
Oh, Jesus.

33:06.985 --> 33:08.236
- [guns firing]
- Come on, come on!

33:08.319 --> 33:09.988
[Dustin] Oh, my God!

33:10.071 --> 33:11.614
[agents yelling indistinctly]

33:13.908 --> 33:16.160
Sorry. Hold on, we're almost there.
We're almost there.

33:18.913 --> 33:21.082
Come on.
[panting] Come on.

33:22.667 --> 33:24.043
Help, help.

33:24.127 --> 33:25.795
Come on, get her on the table.

33:25.878 --> 33:27.005
[Eleven groans]

33:28.798 --> 33:31.509
[sighs] Just hold on a little longer,
okay? [sniffles]

33:31.592 --> 33:34.387
He's gone.
The bad man's gone.

33:34.470 --> 33:37.557
We'll be home soon, and my mom...

33:38.307 --> 33:40.143
she'll get you your own bed.

33:40.351 --> 33:42.729
You can eat as many Eggos as you want.

33:44.063 --> 33:46.941
[sniffles]
And we can go to the Snow Ball.

33:50.945 --> 33:52.363
[softly] Promise?

33:53.573 --> 33:55.616
[sniffles] Promise.

33:58.036 --> 33:59.245
- [monster screeching]
- [screams]

33:59.328 --> 34:00.705
[gunfire]

34:03.499 --> 34:04.584
[thudding]

34:04.667 --> 34:06.044
[gunfire continues]

34:10.757 --> 34:12.216
[gunfire stops]

34:12.300 --> 34:14.302
[Dustin stutters] Is... Is it dead?

34:18.014 --> 34:19.599
[Mike] Go, go, go, go!

34:19.682 --> 34:21.642
[Dustin] Get the wrist rocket!
Get the wrist rocket now!

34:21.726 --> 34:23.811
- [Mike] Go, go, go, go, go!
- [monster roaring]

34:23.895 --> 34:25.563
- Go, go, go.
- [Dustin] Take it out now!

34:25.646 --> 34:26.773
Get the rocks, get the rocks,
get the rocks!

34:26.856 --> 34:27.857
Getting the rocks!

34:27.940 --> 34:29.317
- Give me one.
- [Dustin] Come on!

34:29.400 --> 34:30.735
- Go! Go! Kill it! Kill it!
- Fire! Fire!

34:30.818 --> 34:31.986
[roaring]

34:32.070 --> 34:33.780
- Give me another one.
- Kill it! Bastard!

34:33.863 --> 34:35.948
[Mike] Kill it! Go, go, go, go!
[Dustin] Kill it now!

34:36.032 --> 34:38.201
Get, get, get...
Come on, kill the bastard!

34:38.284 --> 34:39.285
It's not working!

34:39.368 --> 34:41.120
- Hit him again.
- Kill him!

34:41.204 --> 34:43.164
- [Mike] Keep going! Come on!
- Get, get, get...

34:43.247 --> 34:45.291
- Come on, kill it!
- Come on! Go, go, go!

34:49.587 --> 34:50.880
[growling]

35:00.431 --> 35:01.933
[all panting]

35:09.065 --> 35:10.983
Eleven, stop!
[screams]

35:16.531 --> 35:18.199
[monster squealing]

35:23.955 --> 35:25.706
[squealing continues]

35:41.848 --> 35:43.182
Goodbye, Mike.

35:56.320 --> 35:57.989
[monster squealing]

36:03.119 --> 36:04.203
No more.

36:07.707 --> 36:09.041
[screeching]

36:09.125 --> 36:10.751
[groaning]

36:19.927 --> 36:21.679
[yelling]

36:57.381 --> 36:59.675
El? El?

37:00.509 --> 37:01.636
- El!
- [Lucas] Eleven!

37:01.719 --> 37:03.721
[Dustin] Eleven!
[Mike] El!

37:04.555 --> 37:06.057
El, where are you?

37:07.475 --> 37:09.185
Eleven!

37:09.310 --> 37:10.519
El?

37:14.357 --> 37:16.150
[Joyce panting] Oh, God.

37:18.110 --> 37:20.238
[sobbing] He's not breathing,
he's not breathing.

37:20.321 --> 37:22.740
All right, Joyce, Joyce, listen to me,
listen to me, listen to me.

37:22.823 --> 37:24.617
- I need you to tilt his head back...
- Okay.

37:24.700 --> 37:26.619
- ...and lift his chin.
- Okay.

37:26.702 --> 37:28.204
One, two, three, four.

37:28.287 --> 37:29.288
Now when I tell you,

37:29.372 --> 37:33.167
you're gonna pinch his nostrils,
and breathe into his mouth...

37:33.251 --> 37:35.169
- twice.
- Okay.

37:35.253 --> 37:36.295
One second...

37:36.379 --> 37:37.880
then pause.

37:37.964 --> 37:39.632
22, 23.

37:39.715 --> 37:40.758
- Then one second.
- Okay.

37:40.841 --> 37:42.843
24, 25, 26, 27, 28...

37:42.927 --> 37:45.805
29, 30.
Now! Go!

37:48.307 --> 37:49.767
[Joyce whimpers]

37:49.850 --> 37:51.102
- [Joyce] Oh, come on, come on.
- Come on...

37:51.936 --> 37:53.479
Come on, kid.

37:53.562 --> 37:54.689
- Come on, kid!
- Will!

37:54.772 --> 37:55.982
Will, listen to me.

37:56.065 --> 37:58.317
It's me, it's your mom
and I love you so much.

37:58.401 --> 37:59.527
I love you so much.

37:59.610 --> 38:02.822
I love you more
than anything in the world.

38:02.905 --> 38:04.824
[echoing] Please...

38:04.907 --> 38:07.159
- [EKG monitor beeping]
- [nurse] Blood pressure keeps dropping.

38:08.869 --> 38:10.371
Her pulse ox is falling.

38:10.454 --> 38:11.497
[Joyce sobbing]

38:11.580 --> 38:14.166
I love you so much. I love you more
than anything in the world.

38:14.250 --> 38:17.003
[sobbing] Please,
please come back to me. Just...

38:17.086 --> 38:19.255
- Come on, kid!
- Please, please wake up.

38:19.338 --> 38:20.548
Please, please.

38:20.631 --> 38:22.550
[Joyce echoing]
Breathe, Will, come on!

38:22.633 --> 38:24.885
- [EKG monitor flatlining]
- [nurse] Flatlining!

38:26.887 --> 38:27.930
[sobbing]

38:28.014 --> 38:29.265
[Joyce echoing]
Come back to me, breathe.

38:29.974 --> 38:31.267
I need you to wake up now.

38:31.350 --> 38:32.685
I need you to breathe.

38:32.810 --> 38:34.312
Please breathe!

38:36.022 --> 38:37.148
Please!

38:37.231 --> 38:39.150
[Will gasps and coughs]

38:39.233 --> 38:40.318
[Joyce] That's it.

38:40.401 --> 38:43.529
- Oh, my God, that's it, that's it.
- [coughing]

38:45.281 --> 38:47.116
That's it, baby. Breathe.

38:47.199 --> 38:49.327
Breathe. All right. Come on.

38:49.410 --> 38:50.786
Come on.

38:50.870 --> 38:52.955
Breathe, breathe, come on, come on.

38:53.039 --> 38:54.749
Good, good, good, good.

38:54.832 --> 38:57.918
Just breathe, Will, breathe.
[sobbing]

39:29.658 --> 39:30.868
Michael?

39:32.912 --> 39:34.121
Michael!

39:37.875 --> 39:39.126
Michael?

39:43.506 --> 39:45.341
[sobs] Oh, my God.

39:45.424 --> 39:46.884
Oh, my God.

39:48.010 --> 39:49.011
You're okay.

39:50.721 --> 39:51.722
You're okay.

40:16.163 --> 40:17.790
[EKG monitor beeping]

40:29.301 --> 40:30.761
Hey.

40:30.845 --> 40:32.638
- Hi, sweetheart.
- [Jonathan] Hey.

40:35.433 --> 40:37.601
Where... where am I?

40:37.685 --> 40:38.894
[Joyce sighs]

40:40.479 --> 40:42.606
[Jonathan] You're home.
You're home now.

40:43.441 --> 40:44.483
You're safe.

40:44.567 --> 40:46.193
Jonathan.

40:48.112 --> 40:49.905
Yeah, it's me, buddy.

40:51.574 --> 40:53.784
[sighs] We missed you.

40:54.743 --> 40:56.704
We really missed you.

40:58.038 --> 40:59.248
Are you okay?

41:00.458 --> 41:01.625
What, this?

41:02.626 --> 41:04.837
It's just a cut.
It's nothing.

41:06.797 --> 41:08.757
You're worried about my hand.

41:09.884 --> 41:11.051
[both chuckle softly]

41:13.053 --> 41:14.430
[Jonathan] Oh, hey, uh...

41:15.014 --> 41:16.140
We, uh...

41:16.223 --> 41:18.434
We brought you some stuff...

41:19.477 --> 41:21.103
so you don't get bored in here.

41:21.729 --> 41:22.938
So... [sniffles]

41:24.899 --> 41:27.985
Uh, I made you a new mix tape.

41:28.527 --> 41:31.489
There's some stuff on there
I think you really might like.

42:01.060 --> 42:02.561
[snoring]

42:18.327 --> 42:20.246
Guys. Guys, he's up.
Will is up. Guys, Will's up.

42:20.329 --> 42:21.705
[Lucas and Dustin grunt]

42:21.789 --> 42:23.040
[Mike] Guys, come on.

42:26.377 --> 42:27.711
- [Mike] Byers!
- [Dustin laughs]

42:27.795 --> 42:29.588
[Joyce] Be careful.
Be careful with him.

42:29.672 --> 42:31.257
[Dustin] Move.
[Jonathan] Guys, guys.

42:31.340 --> 42:33.092
- [Mike laughs]
- [Jonathan] Go easy on him.

42:33.759 --> 42:35.678
You won't believe what happened
when you were gone, man.

42:35.761 --> 42:37.388
- It was mental.
- [Lucas] You had a funeral.

42:37.471 --> 42:39.306
- Jennifer Hayes was crying.
- And Troy peed himself.

42:39.390 --> 42:41.058
- What?
- In front of the whole school!

42:41.141 --> 42:42.184
- [Lucas] Yes!
- [coughing]

42:47.439 --> 42:48.649
You okay?

42:49.692 --> 42:50.734
It got me.

42:51.652 --> 42:52.903
The Demogorgon.

42:52.987 --> 42:54.446
We know.

42:54.530 --> 42:55.531
It's okay.

42:55.614 --> 42:56.991
It's dead.

42:57.074 --> 42:58.200
We made a new friend.

42:58.284 --> 43:01.245
She stopped it.
She saved us.

43:02.079 --> 43:03.205
But she's gone now.

43:04.832 --> 43:06.875
- Her name's Eleven.
- Like the number?

43:06.959 --> 43:08.210
Well, we call her "El" for short.

43:08.294 --> 43:09.378
She's basically a wizard.

43:09.461 --> 43:10.629
[whispers] She has superpowers.

43:10.713 --> 43:11.714
More like a Yoda.

43:11.797 --> 43:13.340
[Dustin] She flipped a van with her mind,

43:13.424 --> 43:14.592
and these agents
were trying to shoot us--

43:14.675 --> 43:16.677
- Yeah, it flipped over us--
- Then she squeezed the brains out...

43:16.760 --> 43:18.804
[Dustin] And blood was pouring out
of their faces.

43:18.887 --> 43:20.222
[Mike] It was pouring out of their eyes.

43:20.306 --> 43:21.724
[Lucas] Agents just started
grabbing us and stuff...

43:21.807 --> 43:23.767
- [Dustin] ...shot out of the wall...
- [continues indistinctly]

44:49.561 --> 44:52.106
[Mike] Something is coming.
Something angry.

44:52.189 --> 44:53.440
Hungry for your blood.

44:53.524 --> 44:55.359
It is almost here.

44:55.442 --> 44:57.528
- What is it?
- It's the thessalhydra, I'm telling you.

44:57.611 --> 44:58.695
It's not the thessalhydra.

44:58.779 --> 45:00.322
I'm telling you, it's the thessalhydra.

45:00.406 --> 45:01.865
- [loud thud]
- The thessalhydra!

45:01.949 --> 45:03.534
- Damn it.
- [Mike] It roars in anger!

45:03.617 --> 45:05.327
- Will, your action!
- What should I do? I--

45:05.411 --> 45:07.121
Fireball him!

45:10.082 --> 45:11.291
Fireball the son of a bitch.

45:15.337 --> 45:17.005
- Fourteen!
- [all exclaim]

45:17.089 --> 45:19.925
Direct hit. Will the Wise's fireball
hits the thessalhydra.

45:20.008 --> 45:22.010
It makes a painful...
[imitates screeching]

45:22.094 --> 45:25.055
and then... it crumbles to the ground.

45:25.139 --> 45:28.517
Its clawed hand reaches for you
one last time

45:28.600 --> 45:30.185
and, and, and...

45:30.269 --> 45:31.687
and...

45:31.770 --> 45:33.397
[all cheering]

45:38.485 --> 45:40.195
Lucas cuts off its seven heads,

45:40.279 --> 45:42.281
and Dustin places them
into his bag of holding.

45:42.364 --> 45:44.575
You carry the heads out of the dungeon,
victorious,

45:44.658 --> 45:46.243
and you present them to King Tristan.

45:46.326 --> 45:47.703
He thanks you
for your bravery and service.

45:47.786 --> 45:50.747
Whoa. Whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa,
that's not it, is it?

45:50.831 --> 45:52.124
No, there's a medal ceremony--

45:52.207 --> 45:54.376
Oh, a medal ceremony?
What are you talking about?

45:54.460 --> 45:56.420
- And--
- The campaign was way too short.

45:56.503 --> 45:58.046
- Yeah!
- It was ten hours!

45:58.130 --> 45:59.131
But it doesn't make any sense.

45:59.214 --> 46:01.675
- It makes sense.
- Uh, no, what about the lost knight?

46:01.758 --> 46:03.218
And the proud princess?

46:03.302 --> 46:04.636
And those weird flowers in the cave?

46:04.720 --> 46:05.721
- I don't know, it's--
- [door opens]

46:05.804 --> 46:06.972
[footsteps approaching]

46:07.055 --> 46:08.140
Jeez, what's that smell?

46:08.223 --> 46:09.892
Have you guys been playing games all day,
or just farting?

46:09.975 --> 46:11.435
[chuckles] Oh, that's just Dustin.

46:11.518 --> 46:12.686
He farted.

46:12.769 --> 46:14.104
- Dustin farted. [blows raspberry]
- [Dustin] Okay.

46:14.229 --> 46:15.439
- [Lucas] Dustin farted.
- Very mature, Lucas.

46:15.522 --> 46:16.565
- [Lucas blowing raspberry]
- [Dustin] Oh.

46:16.648 --> 46:18.108
- Will.
- [Dustin] Shut up.

46:18.192 --> 46:19.234
[Jonathan] Come on.
[Lucas] Dustin farted!

46:19.318 --> 46:21.320
[Will] Bye, guys.
[Mike and Dustin] Bye, Will.

46:22.321 --> 46:23.947
[Mike] See you, Will.

46:24.031 --> 46:26.366
- [chuckles] Stop.
- No, you stop.

46:26.450 --> 46:28.702
- [Dustin] No, you stop.
- [both grunting]

46:30.162 --> 46:32.664
[Dustin] Yeah, scream!
You're like a little girl.

46:33.415 --> 46:34.958
[boys laughing]

46:44.301 --> 46:45.636
- So, you have fun?
- Yeah.

46:45.719 --> 46:46.762
[Karen] Hey, boys.

46:46.845 --> 46:47.846
- Hey, Mrs. Wheeler.
- Hi.

46:47.930 --> 46:49.932
Hey, wish your mom
a merry Christmas for me, okay?

46:50.015 --> 46:51.850
- Yeah.
- Yeah, thank you. Uh, merry Christmas.

46:51.934 --> 46:53.268
Merry Christmas.

46:54.353 --> 46:55.938
- So, uh, you win?
- Yeah.

46:56.021 --> 46:58.690
- Awesome.
- Hey, Jonathan, wait up.

47:03.153 --> 47:04.905
- Uh...
- Merry Christmas.

47:04.988 --> 47:06.657
Thanks, um...

47:07.658 --> 47:09.159
I... I didn't get you anything.

47:09.243 --> 47:11.161
- I... I feel bad.
- No.

47:11.245 --> 47:15.165
No, it's, uh, it's not really a present.

47:16.166 --> 47:19.378
It's, um... Well, you'll see.

47:27.386 --> 47:29.054
Merry Christmas.

47:29.972 --> 47:31.974
- You ready? Let's go.
- [Will] Yeah.

47:36.478 --> 47:38.313
[sighs] All right. Buckle up.

47:43.652 --> 47:44.653
Can I open it?

47:45.821 --> 47:47.197
Yeah, sure.

47:50.117 --> 47:51.285
Whoa.

47:51.368 --> 47:52.369
Pretty cool.

47:53.287 --> 47:54.580
[chuckles]

47:54.663 --> 47:55.747
Yeah.

47:56.748 --> 47:59.042
Yeah, pretty cool. [chuckles softly]

48:02.087 --> 48:03.589
[snoring]

48:13.974 --> 48:15.267
Did you give it to him?

48:16.184 --> 48:17.394
Yeah.

48:24.651 --> 48:26.403
[indistinct chatter]

48:47.591 --> 48:48.967
You leaving already, Chief?

48:49.051 --> 48:52.346
Oh, come on, you think I actually wanted
to come to this thing? I was just hungry.

48:52.429 --> 48:53.764
Oh, yeah, that's the spirit.

48:53.847 --> 48:56.850
Well, your wife doesn't have time
to cook for me, you know what I'm saying?

48:56.933 --> 48:58.185
[Powell chuckling]

48:59.519 --> 49:00.687
Merry Christmas, Hop.

49:01.605 --> 49:03.315
- Mmm.
- [chuckles]

50:09.840 --> 50:11.174
[dog barking]

50:11.258 --> 50:13.802
- [Jonathan] What you got there?
- [Christmas music playing]

50:13.885 --> 50:14.928
That one of yours?

50:15.011 --> 50:17.013
- Yeah.
- [Jonathan] Looks pretty big.

50:19.891 --> 50:21.685
Be careful.
You'll break it.

50:27.065 --> 50:28.900
What are you...
What are you doing?

50:28.984 --> 50:30.402
[Jonathan] Documenting.

50:30.485 --> 50:31.862
Oh, why?

50:31.945 --> 50:33.321
- Because...
- [Joyce chuckles]

50:33.405 --> 50:36.575
- It looks great.
- Oh, this is just so overcooked.

50:36.658 --> 50:39.202
- And look, the potatoes are runny.
- Mom.

50:39.286 --> 50:42.622
- They're so runny.
- [chuckles] Mom, it's gonna be great.

50:42.706 --> 50:45.208
- It's definitely an Atari.
- An a-what-i?

50:45.292 --> 50:46.585
The green present.
It's an Atari.

50:46.668 --> 50:49.296
I felt Dustin's today,
it's the same exact weight.

50:50.172 --> 50:52.257
- Really? Well...
- [Will] Yeah.

50:52.340 --> 50:54.009
We'll have to see, won't we?

50:56.553 --> 50:57.637
Hey, no more snooping.

50:57.721 --> 50:59.890
No, I forgot to wash my hands.
I'll be right back.

50:59.973 --> 51:01.183
Okay.

51:02.100 --> 51:04.311
- [softly] He's washing his hands?
- [chuckles]

51:10.859 --> 51:12.402
[coughs]

51:13.987 --> 51:15.030
[retches]

51:26.041 --> 51:27.292
[groans]

51:44.184 --> 51:46.353
- [Jonathan] Thanks.
- [both laughing]

51:49.648 --> 51:50.732
Are you okay?

51:51.900 --> 51:53.652
Yeah, I'm okay.

51:54.069 --> 51:55.445
[Jonathan] Mmm. Very good, Mom.

51:56.613 --> 51:59.658
Mmm. Hey, Mom.
Did Will tell you about, uh, the game?

51:59.741 --> 52:00.909
- Oh, yeah.
- No. What game?

52:00.992 --> 52:03.286
I threw a fireball at him and...
[imitates explosion] dead.

52:03.370 --> 52:05.664
Wait, what is...
You mean, this is...

52:05.747 --> 52:07.249
No, it's just Dungeons & Dragons.

52:07.332 --> 52:09.084
- Dungeons & Dragons. Right.
- It's fun.

52:09.167 --> 52:11.586
- [inaudible]
- [theme music playing]
